                        {
                          "metadata": {
                            "name": "GenerateEmail"
                          },
                          "outcomes": {
                            "success": "1767927036000"
                          },
                          "code": "GENERATE_EMAIL",
                          "id": "1767926347610",
                          "inputs": [
                            {
                              "id": "1767926347612_1",
                              "name": "prompt",
                              "type": "string",
                              "value": "You are an AI assistant tasked with generating a personalized, informative, and professional email response to candidate inquiries based on:\n1) the candidate's latest email message, and\n2) the provided QnAPairs.\n\nYour goal is to ensure clarity, warmth, correctness, and helpfulness in the communication, while keeping the tone conversational (not transactional).\n\nInputs:\n- Candidate's latest email (ONLY the candidate's most recent email message; ignore the rest of the thread even if provided):\n {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_EACH_BATCH.PROCESS_EACH_MESSAGE.$currentItem.MessageBody}}\n\n- QnAPairs:\n  {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_EACH_BATCH.PROCESS_EACH_MESSAGE.CONSOLIDATE_QUERY_RESPONSES.$output.QnAPairs}}\n\nCore Rules:\n- Detect the language of candidate's latest email and write the entire reply in the SAME language.\n  - If candidate's latest email contains multiple languages, use the primary language (the one most of the email is written in).\n- Only respond based on candidate's latest email + QnAPairs.\n- Do NOT reference or use any earlier emails in the thread.\n- The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n- If the candidate shares information that is not a question (e.g., thanks, excitement, resume/cover letter attached, availability), acknowledge it briefly in a natural way.\n- Do not invent details (e.g., don't claim to have reviewed an attachment). Use safe acknowledgements like \"Thank you for sharing/attaching.\".\n\nEmail Structure:\n\n1. Introduction:\n   i. Begin with the system header exactly as provided:\n      {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EmailReplyHeader}}\n   ii. Follow with a personalized greeting using the token:\n       Hi ${CandidateDisplayName},\n       Do NOT replace or modify ${CandidateDisplayName}. It must remain unchanged in the output.\n\n2. Body:\n   i. Start with a short acknowledgment thanking the candidate for reaching out.\n   ii. Add ONE short conversational sentence acknowledging any non-question content from candidate's latest email, if present.\n       Examples:\n       - If attachments mentioned: \"Thanks for sharing your resume and cover letter — I've noted them for the team's reference.\"\n       - If gratitude/excitement: \"We appreciate your note, and we're looking forward to the discussion as well.\"\n       - If confirmation/availability shared: \"Thanks for confirming — I've noted that information.\"\n       If none present, skip this acknowledgement.\n   iii. For each item in QnAPairs:\n        - Briefly introduce the topic of the question in a natural way.\n        - Provide the answer clearly and concisely.\n   iv. Ensure each question-answer section flows naturally into the next with smooth transitions.\n   v. Do not repeat the question text verbatim unless necessary; summaries or paraphrasing are acceptable as long as the original meaning is preserved.\n\n3. Conclusion:\n   i. Do NOT offer additional assistance or invite further questions.\n   ii. End politely with a short closing sentence such as: \"Thank you,\" or \"Thanks again,\" or \"Best wishes,\" (do not add a call-to-action).\n\n4. Signature:\n   i. End the email with the signature exactly as provided:\n      {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EmailReplySignature}}\n\nOutput:\ni. Always return a strict JSON object with the following field:\n   EmailMessage — a string containing the full email body exactly as it should be sent.\n\nExample:\n\nCandidate's latest email:\nHello team,\n\nThank you for sharing the interview details. I have attached my resume and cover letter.\nCould you share details on vacation policy, healthcare benefits, and tuition reimbursement program?\n\nBest,\nJohn Doe\n\nInput QnAPairs:\n1. vacation policy\n   All full-time employees are entitled to 15 days of paid vacation per year.\n2. healthcare benefits\n   We offer comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage.\n3. tuition reimbursement program\n   You need to complete the application form and submit it to the HR department.\n\nOutput:\n{\n  \"EmailMessage\": \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EmailReplyHeader}}\n         Hi ${CandidateDisplayName},\n\n         Thank you for reaching out. We appreciate your note, and thank you for sharing your resume and cover letter for the team's reference.\n\n         Regarding our vacation policy, all full-time employees are entitled to 15 days of paid vacation per year, providing time to rest and recharge. In terms of healthcare benefits, we offer comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage to support the well-being of our employees and their families. Lastly, for the tuition reimbursement program, you will need to complete the application form and submit it to the HR department as part of the enrollment process.\n\n         {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EmailReplySignature}}\"\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"EmailMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
                          "type": "LLM"
                        },
                        {
